  "material_note": "songk3crystal_R: pink crystal, MU's bright sheet, the Ruins' own (kr_songk3crystal_r.png, byte-identical): lamplight, drawn added.",
  "why_this_one": "A pink crystal cluster rising out of the void round the whole maze, 69 of them. MU places 5 by the safe hall at floor height (three on the strips the Relics no longer draw, 95e5d554). Ours: all sunk to -7 m so the bases vanish in the abyss's dark and the tips show 4.6 m under the floor, below the void clouds (the user, 2026-10-24: \"they have to be lower and bottom part is almost invissible like they are coming from voide\", \"more lower ... also we need smoke layer coming above crystals levels\"), and 64 more laid round the maze 3-6 tiles off its edge, 10 tiles apart, turned and sized 0.6-0.9 at random (\"lets put more crystals around whole platform\"). Its geometry is the Ruins' Object96, vertex for vertex. Batch 8 of the Relics. docs/worlds/kanturu-port.md Part B 8.1.",
  "additive": [
    "songk3crystal_R"
  ],
  "additive_from": "An _R sheet: MU's TextureScript marks it bright (TextureScript.cpp:16-58), so it is drawn added. Its chrome pass and its ten blue sparks: glow_from and emitters_from.",
