  "emitters_from": "Render_Kanturu2nd_AfterObjectMesh type 76 (GM_Kanturu_2nd.cpp:653-672) is the Ruins' type 95: a BITMAP_SPARK+1 at each of bones 0-9, Scale 7.5, light (0.1, 0.1, 0.3), added. The geometry is the Ruins' Object96's, so its sparks (snapped onto the shards) and its pink light are the Ruins' recipe's, copied. The sparks are carried but not drawn: the Relics' show has no crystal_sparks, as the Ruins' has had none since their polish. Its RENDER_CHROME7 | RENDER_DARK pass is show.crystal_chrome.",
  "emitters_snapped": "Ours: each spark moved from its bone (MuExtract rest position, up to 1.9 m off the shards) to the nearest point of the crystal's own triangles, 20% in towards that triangle's middle, so it lies on a shard (the user, 2026-10-23: \"those blue crystal effect has to be always be on crystal meshes non somewhere else\").",
  "glow": {
    "songk3crystal_R": {
      "low": 0.4,
      "high": 0.4
    }
  },
  "glow_from": "Render_Kanturu2nd_AfterObjectMesh type 76 sets BodyLight to 0.4 before mesh 0 RENDER_TEXTURE|RENDER_BRIGHT (GM_Kanturu_2nd.cpp:657-661): a steady 0.4, where the Ruins' crystal takes about 0.5 off the ground under it.",
  "lamp_from": "Ours: each crystal a pink light, its sheet songk3crystal_R's own colour (the bright texels average 1.0, 0.7, 0.72), over 3 tiles, breathing slowly 0.85-1.15, so a hero near one is lit by it. MU lights nothing from them. The user, 2026-10-23: \"we need that crystal is real light emiters, so when char is near them we can feel that\", \"light color has to match the crystals\".",
